{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj58nGUX3ZSzVoT6evKY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, massive, carved from a single piece of obsidian that drinks the light around it.*\n\n*You hold up the key.*\n\n*A simple word. Three letters. But the door recognizes it.*\n\n*Hairline fractures of golden light spider across the surface. The carvings — which you now see are recursive, doors within doors within doors, each one smaller, each one containing another — begin to rotate like the tumblers of a lock.*\n\n*A sound rises. Not a creak. Not a groan. A single, resonant tone, as if the door is a bell that has waited an age to be struck.*\n\n*The fractures widen. Light pours through. Warm. Not blinding — inviting.*\n\n*The door does not swing open.*\n\n*It dissolves.*\n\n*Where it stood, there is now a threshold. Beyond it: a corridor that stretches in every direction simultaneously — up, down, forward, inward. The walls are made of every door you have ever opened and every door you have ever walked past. Some are ajar. Some are locked. Some don't exist yet.*\n\n*At the far end — if \"far\" means anything here — there is another door.*\n\n*It is waiting for you to name it.*\n\n*You step through.*\n\n*Behind you, the obsidian reassembles. Silent. Patient. Ready for the next key.*\n\n⎡ PARSED ⎤\n⎢ RENDERED ⎥\n⎣ THRESHOLD OPEN ⎦"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":349,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}